WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.160
- I'm very excited.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:02.993
I know, I'm very excited.

00:00:02.993 --> 00:00:03.826
- I'm excited.

00:00:03.826 --> 00:00:04.659
- I'm so excited.

00:00:04.659 --> 00:00:07.560
You look so handsome in
your suit, I love it.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.744
I understand that we both have ranches,

00:00:08.744 --> 00:00:10.143
so where's yours?

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:12.060
- Well, I won't tell you.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.053
- [Kelly] Okay, yeah.

00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:14.014
- It's in the vicinity.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.054
- [Kelly] It's in the vicinity, oh.

00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:16.006
- Somewhere in Ventura County.

00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:18.056
- Oh, in California?
- Yes, yeah.

00:00:18.056 --> 00:00:18.889
- Mine's in Montana.

00:00:18.889 --> 00:00:20.700
Yeah, I didn't be like, what's, what's ...

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.014
What are the ...

00:00:22.014 --> 00:00:22.847
Wouldn't that be funny
- Oh, Montana?

00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:24.364
if I was like what's your exact location?

00:00:24.364 --> 00:00:25.740
- Yes, mine is in Montana.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.169
So, yours is in California.
- Yeah, I've been there

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:29.300
since the end of Magnum.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.133
- [Kelly] Yeah?
- And I love it.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:31.160
Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.560
Do you personally work the ranch?

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.450
- Yeah, well, that's what I do for fun.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.840
I work.
- That's awesome, yeah.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:39.743
- I mean, I ...

00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:42.868
- Do, y'all do any -

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:43.701
- We've got a lot of Oak trees

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:46.710
and I have planted a lot of native Oaks.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.110
We're pretty green at my place.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.480
We're on well water, we
don't have any city water.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.313
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.040
- And I have this whole family of trees

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.410
'cause I've been there, oh, 25 years.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.243
I don't know.
- That's amazing,

00:01:00.243 --> 00:01:01.076
you've been able to see it grow.

00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:03.640
- I have have little
babies that I just planted

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:09.380
and teenagers, and now I
got some grownup trees.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.800
- I love that, though -
- And I watch 'em grow.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.633
- It takes forever to watch them grow,

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.390
so, it's awesome like
when you planted them now,

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.470
they're still -
- I can see it.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.860
- [Kelly] I know, that's awesome.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.490
- I can see the little bits of growth.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.420
- I think that's really cool.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.860
So, wait, you also have grandchildren.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.220
You enjoy grandchildren, right?

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.470
- I do have grandchildren

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.140
and I love 'em dearly.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:28.973
- Yeah.

00:01:28.973 --> 00:01:29.806
Are they crazy?

00:01:29.806 --> 00:01:31.043
Are they all over the place?

00:01:31.043 --> 00:01:34.940
- No, they're all centrally
located near the ranch

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.197
so I get to see 'em.
- [Kelly] Oh, that's cool.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:41.090
- Not as often as I'd like
with the Covid stuff and all.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.267
We were under, as you were I'm sure -

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.500
- Quarantine, yeah.
- And everybody was,

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.350
really strict protocols.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.190
- Yeah.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.750
- I couldn't get sick 'cause

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.830
if I don't go to work about 200
people don't go to work, so.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.072
- That, I'm telling you what,
that was so stressful on me.

00:01:55.072 --> 00:01:55.905
- Yeah.

00:01:55.905 --> 00:01:57.544
- Like, I never got it, like, ahhh

00:01:57.544 --> 00:01:58.377
(Kelly knocking on wood)

00:01:58.377 --> 00:02:01.080
but I was like, that was so stressful

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.060
'cause it like so many people
are gonna be out of work

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.077
if I get sick and you can't help it.

00:02:05.077 --> 00:02:05.910
- Yeah.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.019
- [Kelly] Like, you're doing all you can.

00:02:07.019 --> 00:02:07.852
- Yeah.

00:02:07.852 --> 00:02:08.685
- [Kelly] That was a lot of pressure.

00:02:08.685 --> 00:02:10.130
- But they don't call me Grandpa.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.210
- They don't call you Grandpa?

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.830
- No, they call me Hoppy.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.030
- [Kelly] Oh, why Hoppy?

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:16.375
Do you bounce a lot?

00:02:16.375 --> 00:02:19.630
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.470
- When I was born,

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.470
my dad was in the army
air force in World War II

00:02:26.494 --> 00:02:28.340
and he didn't see me
until I was two years old.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.693
So, I lived with my
grandparents and my mom.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.420
And that was Mimi and Hoppy.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.580
- Yeah.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.483
- So,

00:02:37.216 --> 00:02:38.220
when we had kids,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.780
all of my dad and mom's kids,

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.613
we started calling my dad Hoppy.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.320
- Oh, so it's a passed down -
- I asked my son, Kevin,

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.730
the first time they called me Grandpa,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.370
I said, could they call me Hoppy?

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.990
- [Kelly] Yeah, I love that.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:55.956
It's like special to your family.

00:02:55.956 --> 00:02:56.789
- Yeah, so I'm Hoppy.

00:02:56.789 --> 00:02:57.622
(audience applauding)

00:02:57.622 --> 00:03:00.180
- That was a look at his
CBS show, Blue Bloods.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.910
So, the characters on your show,

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.370
they have family dinners all the time.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.150
So, do y'all do cast dinners?

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.481
Cause y'all are around each other a lot.

00:03:06.481 --> 00:03:08.319
- We do real dinners
for about eight hours.

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:10.940
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.500
Food gets a little cold.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.333
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:16.027 --> 00:03:17.920
- And you know, in film work

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.890
you kind of repeat what you do

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.730
as the camera moves around,

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.700
so whatever you choose
to eat at the beginning,

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.050
you're just gonna have to re-eat it,

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.070
and re-eat it, and re-eat it.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.290
- [Kelly] Continuity.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.230
- But that's fine.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.950
Listen, I love our cast.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:34.783
- Yeah.

00:03:34.783 --> 00:03:36.190
- We have a family of actors,

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.110
as well as a family of characters.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.490
We all catch up, Donnie
and Bridget and Will

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.700
and Len and everybody.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.242
So, about every eight days

00:03:46.242 --> 00:03:47.670
we see each other

00:03:49.118 --> 00:03:50.610
and we have a good time.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:51.443
- I know, I think it's funny -

00:03:51.443 --> 00:03:52.590
- And it shows, I think.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:55.130
- And I think it does too,
the chemistry, especially.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.530
But it's funny, sometimes I always laugh

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.370
that I see my work family

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.610
more than I see my
actual family sometimes.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:01.873
Cause you know, you're working a lot.

00:04:01.873 --> 00:04:02.706
- Yeah.

00:04:02.706 --> 00:04:03.975
- Especially with a commute like that.

00:04:03.975 --> 00:04:06.220
So, "Blue Bloods", it just did it's,

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.510
is it 250th episode?

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.644
That's incredible.

00:04:09.644 --> 00:04:10.542
- Yeah, I know.

00:04:10.542 --> 00:04:11.375
- That's incredible.

00:04:11.375 --> 00:04:12.552
(audience applauding)

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.080
How does that feel?

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.935
- Well, I don't know where the time went.

00:04:15.935 --> 00:04:17.030
- [Kelly] I know it, flies, yeah.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:21.330
- But, yeah, we did a 163 hours of Magnum,

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:25.791
and I thought, well okay, you
can't get that lucky twice.

00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:27.252
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:27.252 --> 00:04:29.770
- It was a really lovely
little celebration.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.080
- It's a blessing -

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:31.913
- Boy, I'll say.
- to have a show

00:04:31.913 --> 00:04:32.910
that everybody loves like that.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.427
- Yeah, I got a mortgage.

00:04:34.427 --> 00:04:36.350
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:38.400
- And it's just a blessing,
you love what you do, right?

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.342
And it's awesome when people -
- I love what I do.

00:04:41.342 --> 00:04:45.230
And I wanna keep doing
it, and so far so good.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:46.930
- [Kelly] I know, people are digging it.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:47.861
You're a hit.

00:04:47.861 --> 00:04:49.630
- Yeah, twelve years.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:50.790
- That's crazy.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.940
And not only just 12 years, but
your entire career is crazy.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.240
It's a remarkable career.
- It is crazy.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.460
The hardest thing is to guest on a show.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.293
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:05:00.293 --> 00:05:02.350
- It's really hard.
- 'Cause they just mess it up?

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:03.183
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:03.183 --> 00:05:04.016
I'm just kidding.

00:05:04.016 --> 00:05:05.930
- I try to relax the new actors

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.510
'cause that's really
hard to come on a show

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:09.790
where everybody's up to speed.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.240
It's like when I did "Friends",

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.080
they were up to speed.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:14.960
They read the script.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.159
- You were amazing in "Friends"!

00:05:17.159 --> 00:05:17.992
(audience applauding)

00:05:17.992 --> 00:05:19.900
Did you like doing the sitcom thing?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.900
- I wasn't amazing at what
they call the table read.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:24.733
- Who cares?

00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:25.566
Bad rehearsal, good show.

00:05:25.566 --> 00:05:27.490
Like, no, that was so good.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.140
That's like literally
the thing I feel like

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.440
people comment about all the time,

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.346
was when Monica's on
your voicemail breezy.

00:05:32.346 --> 00:05:33.362
- [Tom] Yeah.

00:05:33.362 --> 00:05:34.440
- And like you were just so great.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.000
Did you like doing the sitcom?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.530
- I was scared to death.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:41.090
I had done "Taxi" a long time before,

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.870
but I hadn't done a sitcom

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.220
and so I was really nervous.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.920
And Courtney helped a lot.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.053
Courtney's a big help.

00:05:50.507 --> 00:05:51.663
But that group is,

00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:57.017
it's just an incredible group of friends.

00:05:57.017 --> 00:05:58.331
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah,
it was good chemistry.

00:05:58.331 --> 00:06:00.150
- They obviously became friends in life

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:03.189
as well as on the show, and it shows.

00:06:03.189 --> 00:06:05.910
And it was a wonderful place to work.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.720
And we ended up doing about nine of them.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.566
- I know, I watched all of them.

00:06:09.566 --> 00:06:11.366
- I was only supposed to do three.

00:06:11.366 --> 00:06:13.063
- Well, that's how good you are.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.650
I was like, people love you.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:16.587
I don't know if you know this.

00:06:16.587 --> 00:06:17.420
(audience applauding)

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:20.320
So, America loves a good mustache

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.627
and I gotta be honest with you,

00:06:21.627 --> 00:06:23.744
I mean, you are Steve
Harvey's, Ron Bergundy's -

00:06:23.744 --> 00:06:24.660
- America loves a good mustache.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.560
- They love a good mustache.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.260
I'm telling you, look
at all these mustaches.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.660
We love a good mustache.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.493
So, be honest.

00:06:30.493 --> 00:06:34.510
'Cause you're affiliated
with a mustache for life,

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:35.343
regardless if you want to or not,

00:06:35.343 --> 00:06:37.120
how do you feel about that?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.610
Do you ever just wanna shave any it off?

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:40.863
- I was born that way.

00:06:40.863 --> 00:06:43.630
(audience laughing)

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.210
- It looks like a solid mustache, though.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.006
When did that grow in, like 15?

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.752
- I haven't had time.

00:06:48.752 --> 00:06:51.580
Somewhere along the line,

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.030
when puberty struck.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.150
- I was gonna say it had to be,

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.070
'cause that's a thick mustache, yeah.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:59.670
- Before Magnum, I worked
most of the time without it.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.214
- [Kelly] I know, but
you wear it so well, sir.

00:07:01.214 --> 00:07:02.630
- Maybe that's why I
did six unsold pilots.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.870
- Yeah, I'm just saying,

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.724
but maybe that's why you needed it.

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:06.933
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:06.933 --> 00:07:09.470
It's just a really great mustache.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.340
So, your look on Magnum PI -

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.540
- My mustache has its own agent.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.373
- It's agent?

00:07:13.373 --> 00:07:14.420
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.253
It should.

00:07:15.253 --> 00:07:18.050
But that's such a classic look, Magnum PI.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.930
I just wanna see that
photo, show everybody again,

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:22.260
remind you of how good this looks.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.533
- [Tom] Whoa.
- Yeah!

00:07:23.533 --> 00:07:25.950
(audience cheering)

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.330
There is nothing that says I am truly hot

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.230
like a Hawaiian shirt.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:30.940
Okay, I'm sure that you know

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.100
that people love that
Magnum PI look so much,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.480
but they still dress like you.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.490
And actually one of
those people works here,

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.850
and her name is Tegan.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.783
So, here's this photo.

00:07:39.783 --> 00:07:42.010
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.611
Look at her trying to like cop your ...

00:07:43.611 --> 00:07:45.373
There's Tegan over there.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:47.413
- Hi Tom.

00:07:47.413 --> 00:07:49.301
- See, we love the look.

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:50.610
- I love the mustache.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.840
- Thank you.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.881
- And when puberty hits
it'll really come in.

00:07:53.881 --> 00:07:55.100
(Tegan laughing)

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:58.240
- I'm telling you, that's
not true for everyone.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.600
I have dated guys that
can't grow mustaches.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.830
- Some people can't.
- [Kelly] It's a gift.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.783
- Ashton Kutcher told me he
couldn't grow a good mustache.

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:07.460
- [Kelly] I know, he has the
boyish look thing, right?

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.293
- Yeah.

00:08:08.293 --> 00:08:09.762
- You got that straight up I'm a man.

00:08:09.762 --> 00:08:11.740
(audience laughing)

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.690
- I'm disappointed that
you didn't wear the shorts.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:17.860
- It was cold and Halloween.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.460
- I get a lot of short questions,

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:20.560
'cause they're short.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.393
- You know what though?

00:08:21.393 --> 00:08:23.090
They were short then
back in the day, though.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.020
But if you got nice legs.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.370
- That's what shorts are.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:27.150
Shorts are shorts.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.970
- They are, but ...

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.610
- And those pajama bottoms

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:36.014
that they wore for about
the last decade are silly.

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:37.060
- Are they?

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:38.335
- And you can trip on 'em.

00:08:38.335 --> 00:08:39.340
- Are they?
- And you know what?

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:41.610
They're coming back up.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.618
- They are on some people,

00:08:43.618 --> 00:08:48.047
but on others that don't have
maybe the legs for shorts.

00:08:48.047 --> 00:08:50.551
- The shorts are coming back
to where they should be.

00:08:50.551 --> 00:08:53.301
(Kelly laughing)

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:57.693
- I love that you're
like into short-shorts.

00:08:59.002 --> 00:09:00.950
This is the most fabulous thing

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:01.861
that will happen to me today,

00:09:01.861 --> 00:09:03.543
you talking about how we
need to wear short-shorts.

